History of Brazil (@history-of-brazil: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_46RA9VDE0BW8156A5J17T2P67Q
This material investigates Brazil's historical formation through work, slavery and abolition, institutions, state formation, regions, cities, economic transformations, political struggles, and cultural life. Develop routes across colonial, imperial, republican, and contemporary periods with explicit source criticism and attention to differences of place and social position. Connect Brazilian literature, philosophical debates, sociological research, and Political-Economy to the conditions in which their questions emerged. Compare interpretations instead of presenting one narrative as the only possible account.

